      "content": "Yes, grain orientation is very important in dovetails. You want the taper of your pins to run consistently along the grain to support the cut effectively. When cutting, try to keep the direction of your chisel strokes consistently across the grain rather than fighting against the grain with your initial cuts. This slight adjustment in angle often helps prevent the delicate tips from splintering.",
