      "content": "Walnut's density and varying moisture content can certainly make it challenging, especially in edges. If the cut is happening consistently in one area, check that you are dulling or scoring the wood slightly *before* the final precise cut to give your tool something to follow. Sometimes a slight flattening or \"smoothing\" of the wood surface before sawing can drastically reduce tear-out.",
